    "id": 22676798,
    "hashId": "1L8EEq",
    "name": "Manor in the Fields",
    "description": "<p>Lately I've been wanting to tend more towards realism / photorealism, so I'm mostly practicing proper exposure values, proper asset lookdev and more. After talking with Lucas Piazzini, he shared some fun lookdev tips I wanted to try right away, and ended up making a little scene with those assets. It's a pretty modest environment, nothing fancy; done in 2-3 hours, but I'm happy with how it looks!</p>",
